@@ -70,6 +70,26 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Use it when you want raw text output and do not want Rich's formatting applied.
+
+``out`` does the following:
+
+- Writes plain text without pretty printing of containers or objects.
+- Does not word wrap or crop output to the console width.
+- Does not interpret console markup or replace emoji codes.
+- Applies highlighting by default (``highlight=True``); pass ``highlight=False`` to disable it, or ``None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+- Applies a basic ``style`` if one is given.
+
+Example::
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold]Hello[/bold]", "World", sep=" ", end="!\n")
+
+Output still passes through the normal print pipeline, so render hooks and capture work as they do for print.
+
+
